From d0de333e59bb44049e9dc11568b11d59d483150e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tsm-consultz <brightmindsfinancial@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 21:36:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire up TSM Capability Sweep capture + render across 6
 verticals
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every war-room call site to POST /api/enterprise/capability-sweep was
fire-and-forget (fetch(...).catch(...) with no .then()), so the real
caseId + decisionPackage returned by the endpoint was thrown away and
never shown to anyone.

- Add html/shared/tsm-capability-sweep.js: fire() captures the response,
  writes it to localStorage under TSM_<VERTICAL>_CAPABILITY_SWEEP, and
  dispatches TSM_CAPABILITY_SWEEP_READY. render()/renderFromStorage()
  show exactly what came back — no invented phase values; errors,
  context-only phases, and pending phases are labeled honestly.

- Swap the dead fetch(...).catch(...) call for TSMCapabilitySweep.fire()
  in the 6 real call sites: RE, Construction, Legal, Healthcare,
  Insurance, FinOps war rooms.

- Add a "Enterprise Capability Sweep · 10-Phase Case Status" panel to
  each vertical's actual escalation destination (confirmed via each
  war room's window.location.href), so the captured decision package
  is actually rendered where the user lands:
    re-strategist.html, construction-strategist.html,
    legal-main-strategist.html, executive-portal.html (healthcare),
    insurance-strategist.html, finops-main-strategist.html

- legal-main-strategist.html: added missing .sec.cyan CSS rule
  (var(--cyan) existed, the class variant didn't).

BPO and backups/ intentionally left untouched — BPO never called this
endpoint to begin with; wiring it in is a separate decision.
